-- `WHEN JUST TRUE` is a match on the payload VALUE, not a binder:
-- post-typecheck a binder is always PatVar (out-of-scope nullary PatApps are
-- rewritten by the scope checker), so a nullary PatApp payload can only be a
-- genuine constructor pattern. The R8 presence-erasure lowering cannot
-- express it (it would silently degrade to a mere presence test — the
-- pre-repair emitter compiled this to `p.waiver is None`, reporting TRUE for
-- JUST FALSE), so it must be refused by name.

DECLARE Purchase
  HAS
    waiver IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@export whether the buyer waived
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE waived p IF
    CONSIDER p's waiver
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
